    "notes": "Excluding GST. Residential ToU CRSTOU: peak 4pm-9pm, saver 11am-4pm, off-peak 9pm-11am, all days, rates from the CitiPower 2026-27 Tariff Summary (final, 7 May 2026; knowledge/documents/citipower/2026-11-10-tariff-summary-2026-27). Small business ToU peak is 9am-9pm workdays. Residential/export CER tariffs and all demand-charge tariffs (CG/CMG/CMGO21/large/HV/sub-transmission) are NOT seeded -- the only available rate source (AER TSS.01 indicative prices) leaves their demand/export components as zero/blank, and this schema's single demand-window model can't represent CitiPower's two-season (summer/non-summer) demand charge without inventing a modeling choice not made unilaterally. Source PDF gives tariff codes/structure but not $ rates -- those live in the CitiPower 2026-27 Tariff Summary (final, 7 May 2026), which gives CRSTOU rates; rates for the other tariffs here are still sourced from AER's regulator-hosted TSS.01 indicative-prices spreadsheet (2026-31 Tariff Structure Statement, Jan2025 proposal), cross-checked against the structural PDF's tariff codes (exact match: C1R, CDS, CRSTOU, C1G, CGTOU). 'Indicative' prices, not a final DNSP-published price list -- flagged as a slightly different provenance tier than other seeded DNSPs.",
    "last_verified": "2026-08-03"
  },
